					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2198340&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608498386" alt="Kakroom" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2198340)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;" >Kakroom</a></span> <span class="odate time_1481831739 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Dec 2016 19:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2710140">
									

<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Dakiwhat,&quot; Darnell spat, nearly choking on his coffee. &quot;What the fuck is that?&quot;</p>
<p>Quinn decided not to tell him, for two reasons: 1) to spare him from the horror, and 2) in order to see the reaction on his face when he did figure it out.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I never asked you this in chat and I probably should've: why is a discovery of this quality particularly disconcerting? From the brief search I made, all it seems to be is a Japanese love pillow. I can think of about a thousand things more disturbing, many of them related to the country. Is that because I fail to grasp the social implications of the item, or that I just have a really sick mind?</p>
<p>I have no questions beyond that, though. Very fun read.</p>

							</div>

								
